### How the fourteen data sessions work

*Every Thursday takes **one source of data** and goes behind a number you have
already seen. The order is cumulative: nothing is inferred from a source you
have not already met. Voter files come before we guess race from them; precinct
returns come before we infer how groups voted.*

*Each session asks the same five questions — **what is one row? who made this,
and why? how do you get it? what can it settle? what can it never settle?** —
and each has its own reading, due before class, about that data.*

